CONFORMANCE.md §4: `@ts(bigint)` is not supported on a parameter of the pure function, a field read from self included.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A wallet.
record Wallet {
  /// Its balance.
  balance: UInt64 @ts(bigint)

  /// Whether n fits.
  export fn fits(self, n: Int) -> Bool { return balance >= n }
}

emit ts { out: "@features/a/a.ts" }
-- findings.txt --
error[E9006]  a/a.canon:9:49
  Wallet.fits reads balance of type UInt64 through self: translated functions read Bool, integers, Float, Float32, String, Duration and enums from self, never a ref or a @ts(bigint) field; pass the value the body needs as a parameter

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
